codex
Implemented the native Track B generator based on the paper’s balanced Plücker-coordinate invariants ([full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2603.09869v2)).

Local results:

- G1–G8 pass.
- Five attacks fail 0/8.
- Reference projective-frame enumeration solves 8/8 using 1,521,720 counted operations.
- Compact Plücker route uses 288 operations.
- G9 size caps pass: 134 characters, 36 atoms.
- G9(b) and STEP 4 remain unverified because all 12 OpenRouter calls returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” No API error was counted as an oracle failure.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.09869/gen_2603_09869.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.09869/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.09869/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.09869/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.09869/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.09869/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The family is intentionally marked not shippable (`all_passed: false`), not rejected. Once OpenRouter quota is restored, rerun the bare harness, adopt its shipping preset, then rerun both G9 arms at that preset.
