codex
Built a self-contained Track B generator based on Sections 2.3, 3.1, and 4 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2603.09869).

Deliverables:

- [gen_2603_09869.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.09869/gen_2603_09869.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.09869/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.09869/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.09869/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.09869/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.09869/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All nine currently gated checks pass.
- Guessing: 0/200,000.
- Five attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Complete reference algorithm: 8/8, median 220,818 field operations.
- Compact Plücker route: 288 operations.
- Answer: 134 characters, 36 elements.
- Canonical-key invariance: 80/80; unrelated keys: 20/20.

The result is not yet shippable: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” for every oracle request. Those transcript entries are error evidence, not model failures, so STEP 4 has no hardness verdict. After replenishing the key, rerun:

```bash
cd /home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.09869
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_2603_09869.py
```

No `REJECTED.md` was created because this is an infrastructure block, not a G/H/V failure.
