codex
The first implementation is now generating exact finite-field code instances and the planted answers verify independently through all four Vandermonde minors. The hard preset uses \(k=126\), matching the paper’s stated cryptographic-scale lower bound, while the certificate remains one residue; I’m benchmarking the honest dense-elimination reference path and checking relabelling invariance next.
